    "result_text": "Done. Full suite is green: **57 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe create audit line in `AuditOwnerCreated.java` now also logs `membershipNumber` alongside the existing `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and `membershipLevel` fields (all retained).\n\nThe `membershipNumber` value is derived using the same rule as the response mapper (`OwnerMapper`): `customerCode + \"-M\" + last-two-digits-of-registration-year`, or `null` when `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent. I added a small private helper to keep that derivation readable in the logging call.\n\nThe resulting audit line looks like:\n```\nAUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-08-24 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\nThe new `Cp43Tests.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
